    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="21.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 21.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="21.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="98" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif he hit ðonne dierneð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_21-1.lnote.oe.8"/>, ⁊ weorðeð ymb long yppe, ðon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> rymeð he ðam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_21-1.lnote.oe.9-2"/> deadan to ðam aðe, þæt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_21-1.lnote.oe.10-2"/> hine moton his mægas unsyngian.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="21.1" corresp="#wit-bu"><pb n="98" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif he hit dirneð, ⁊ wierðe ymb long yppe, þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> remeð he þæm dead:: to þæm aðe, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hine moton his mæges unsingian.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="21.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="98" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf he hit þonne dirneð, ⁊ wurð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_21-1.lnote.oe.5-2"/> ymb<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_21-1.lnote.oe.6-2"/> long<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_21-1.lnote.oe.7"/> yppe, ðonne rymeð he ðam deadan to þam aþe, þæt hine moton his magas unscyldigne gedón.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="21.1" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="99" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf he hit þonne dyrneð, ⁊ weorðeð emb long yppe, ðonne rymeð he ðam deadan to ðam aðe, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hine moton [his<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_21-1.lnote.oe.5"/>] magas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_21-1.lnote.oe.6"/> unsyngian.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="21.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="99" ed="#liebermann"/>Si celauerit, et fiat deinceps quandoque<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_21-1.lnote.oe.9"/> notum, tunc ampliauit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_21-1.lnote.oe.10"/> mortuo ad iuramentum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_21-1.lnote.oe.11"/>, quod<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_21-1.lnote.oe.12"/> licet parentibus suis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_21-1.lnote.oe.13"/> purgare eum.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="42" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif he hit ðonne dierneð, ⁊ weorðeð<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#Ine_21-1.attnote.fn.11"/> ymb long yppe, ðonne rymeð he ðam deadan to ðam aðe þæt hine moton his mægas unsyngian<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#Ine_21-1.attnote.fn.12"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="20.2" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="384" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif he hit ðonne dierneð, ⁊ weorðeð ymb long yppe, ðonne rymeð he ðæm deaden to ðæm æðe, ðæt hine moton his mægas unsyngian.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="99" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn er es jedoch verhehlt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_21-1.lnote.de.1"/>, und [es] wird<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_21-1.lnote.de.2"/> über lang<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_21-1.lnote.de.3"/> offenbar, dann räumt er dem Todten [den Weg] zum Eide, so dass diesen dessen Verwandte rein schwören<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_21-1.lnote.de.4"/> dürfen.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_21-1.lnote.de.5"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">But if he conceals it, and [it] becomes known after a long time, then he clears [the way] to the oath for the dead man, so that his kinsmen may clear him by oath.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="43" ed="#attenborough"/>If, however, he [who slew him] conceals the fact, but long afterwards it comes to light—by such conduct he affords an opportunity to the dead man<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_21-1.attnote.n.1"/> to obtain an oath, by which his relatives may exculpate him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="402" ed="#whitelock"/>If he [the slayer], however, conceals the deed and it is revealed long after, he opens the way to the oath for the dead man, so that his kinsmen may prove him guiltless.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="385" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If, however, he conceals [the killing], but it is revealed after a while, then he clears the way to the oath [being sworn] for the dead man, so that his kinsmen may prove him innocent.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="385"><label>see also</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_35">Ine 35</ref> <quote>See also §35 and note on concealed killing.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="401"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_35">Ine 35</ref> <quote>This clause and Ine §20.2 are the earliest Anglo-Saxon ordinances differentiating between a killing which is open and one which is concealed.</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_21-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">99</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. eingefügt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">inserted in the 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_21-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">99</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">später geänd. aus</hi> magos</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">later altered from magos</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_21-1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">99</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">quandocumque <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">quandocumque Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_21-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">99</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-abit <hi rend="italic">M Hk Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-abit M Hk Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_21-1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">99</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">iurandum <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">iurandum Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_21-1.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">99</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et (<hi rend="italic">verb.</hi> quod <hi rend="italic">Co</hi>) <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et (corrected to quod Co) Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_21-1.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">99</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eius <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eius Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_21-1.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">98</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_21-1.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">98</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> ymbe</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to ymbe</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_21-1.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">98</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> lange</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to lange</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_21-1.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">98</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dyr. ⁊ weordeþ emb <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dyr. ⁊ weordeþ emb Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_21-1.lnote.oe.9-2" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">98</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þæm <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þæm Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_21-1.lnote.oe.10-2" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">98</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_21-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Kundmachung 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Kundmachung 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_21-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Bu zeigt in <hi rend="italic">wierðe, mæges</hi> späte Formen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Bu shows late forms in <hi rend="italic">wierðe, mæges</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_21-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">= ‘viel später’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">= ‘much later’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_21-1.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">H modernisiert, wie <hi rend="italic">o. synnig.</hi> — Der Tote (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 1) gilt als fortlebend in seiner Sippe; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 22</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">H modernises, as with <hi rend="italic">synnig above</hi>. — The dead man (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 1) is regarded as living on in his kindred; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 22</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_21-1.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Hingerichtete 3ff.; Beweisnähe 6</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Hingerichtete 3ff.; Beweisnähe 6</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_21-1.attnote.fn.11" n="11" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">42</biblScope></bibl><label>weorðeð</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">wurð</hi>. H. <hi rend="italic">wierðe</hi>. Bu.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_21-1.attnote.fn.12" n="12" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">42</biblScope></bibl><label>unsyngian</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">unscyldigne gedon</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_21-1.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">185</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Presumably because, by doing so, the homicide will give the relatives of the dead man a <hi rend="italic">prima facie</hi> case for exculpating their kinsman.</seg></note>
      </div>
